{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2008-12-17","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2017-03-31","@type":"4"}],"/activity-status@code":"4","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/department/narrative":[{"1":"ESA","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/email":[{"1":"f.rispoli@ifad.org"}],"/job-title/narrative":[{"1":"Country Director","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Rispoli, Francesco","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"The programme's overall goal is to reduce poverty, increase incomes and contribute to the overall economic development of poor rural households in Swaziland. Its objectives are to: (i) provide rural poor men and women with access to efficient, effective and sustainable financial services; (ii) develop an enabling and enhanced environment for business development in rural areas; and (iii) establish and/or develop micro and small-scale enterprises (on- and off-farm) as well as business services in rural areas.Policy and institutional objectivesThe programme will improve the business and financial sectors, providing an enabling environment through the reform of policies, regulations, legislation and processes. It will also build the capacity of the public and private sectors and civil society. Access to business and financial services will help stimulate rural economic growth.","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A01"},{"@code":"A07"},{"@code":"A08"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"Zambia 2000001405: E-SAPP Interim (Mid-term) Review Report August 2022","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"@format":"APPLICATION/PDF","@url":"https://operations.ifad.org/documents/654016/b2bd5dc2-c4af-4d9c